      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "670ee779346ff2ff63f5dd76",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'm bumping this.\n\nReceiver-side filters would help a lot, but they do not address the source of the issue. Some groups are mass-inviting strangers, and it has become constant. Just this week I've received 3 invites, and it's only Tuesday.\n\nI’m receiving tons of group invites from accounts I have never met or shared an instance with. Even a low acceptance rate rewards this behavior because some people genuinely end up joining it. \n\nSee: \n\nhttps://vrc.group/HGOD.8615\n\nhttps://vrc.group/CREATE.6614\n\nhttps://vrc.group/303PUB.0430\n\nhttps://vrc.group/GRAVE.9310\n\nhttps://vrc.group/ECSTY.1631\n\nhttps://vrc.group/SANRIO.4744\n\nThese are just some of the groups and most of them have thousands of members.\n\nI think VRChat should:\n\n- Restrict newly created and low-reputation accounts to inviting friends or users they recently shared an instance with.\n\n- Rate-limit invitations per sender and per group, with higher limits granted to established accounts and groups with strong reputation and clean moderation history.\n\n- Apply spam protection at group level. Sender-only limits can be bypassed by rotating through multiple invite-capable members.\n\n- Detect invitation bursts, unusually high unique-recipient counts, and high decline, block, or report rates.\n\n- Temporarily freeze suspicious invitation activity and flag repeated or high-confidence abuse for manual review.\n\n- Show legitimate group administrators clear cooldown errors instead of silently triggering API suspensions with unclear error messages.\n\n- Keep receiver-side controls as a final backstop, but stop abuse before thousands of unwanted notifications are delivered.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
